            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdominal pain as a leading symptom for Degos' disease (malignant atrophic papulosis).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1098-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 16-yr-old white female patient with acute abdominal pain due to visceral involvement of Degos' disease that required extensive small bowel resection. Skin manifestations of her disease had been present for 2 yr before the correct diagnosis. She died as a result of central nervous system involvement from Degos' disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
